<title>GERMANY: GERMAN GRAIN TRADE SEEKS FREE MKT BARLEY EXPORT.</title>
<headline>GERMAN GRAIN TRADE SEEKS FREE MKT BARLEY EXPORT.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids for the export of 3,400 tonnes of free market barley with rebates in a range between 11.38 and 14.02 ecus per tonne, state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>No other free market bids were received from the German trade for consideration by the EU cereals management committee meeting later Thursday.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
